    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nA while back, in the late 1930's if memory serves me correct, I filed a bug report about not wanting `mini.trailspace` to activate in `mini.starter`, which you resolved.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, I'd like `MiniMisc.find_root()` to run on `mini.starter` buffers (99% of the time I pick the starter entry that spawns a Telescope file browser for `$PWD`, so I'd like pwd to be set right away).\r\n\r\nThe issue is that I don't see anything in `mini-starter.txt` that shows for dummies like me what `mini.starter`'s events are. Could you maybe clarify what event I'm looking for for creating an autocommand that runs when `mini.starter` opens a buffer?\r\n\r\nHooking into starter's behaviour opens up some fun possibilities, so perhaps this is an opportunity for highlighting the documentation of starter's event hooks?",
    "closed_at": "2023-01-06T15:05:56Z",
    "closed_by": {
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2219761?v=4",
